  "evidence": [
    "Pinned setup_faction_data481FD0 reads93D4F0 at48200A and93D4F4 at48200F; pick_pass47C970 reads same addresses at47C9CE/47CEE6. NetDaemonNet begins93CD90, therefore exact offsets760/764. Net constructor62D6A0 zeros those fields at62D84A/62D850; close62E010 does so at62E02C/62E032. Separate NetWin globals cannot represent that shared original storage.",
    "Pinned join_session62E540 passes this+760 via LEA at62E82A to CreatePlayer. enum_players630C80 host-flag path tests bit0 at630D3B and stores callback DPID to+764 at630D48. drop_player632350 replaces departed host at63260C. Supports local_player_id_ and host_player_id_ names. Preserve DPID/uint32_t types/layout and all error/initialization effects.",
    "Rename both member fields consistently, provide public const typed accessors for derived/external readers, and remove NetWinPlayerId/NetWinOtherPlayerId definitions/declarations. Preserve bit-pattern conversions and explicit existing casts unless separately proven unnecessary. If external writes require protected mutation, preserve real state ownership rather than opening duplicate storage or discarding behavior; report scope discoveries.",
    "Add native Net member offsets760/764 and v3 aliases at93D4F0/93D4F4 beside real NetDaemonNet mapping. Parent remains historically unbounded, no invented whole-object extent. Verify native object reader and fresh compiler offsets; no manual ORIGINAL/claim edits.",
    "Review and update affected actual-source test fixtures, not archival patch files or unrelated protocol assumptions. Add regression demonstrating Net owner state is observed by NetWin consumers and cannot diverge into copies. Require build/link, original matching and claim continuity, physical outside-scope difference review. Structural correction is not a game acceptance or automatic byte restoration claim."
  ],
